From: SBE1V1K build <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] ssdk_init: port DSA events to 6.12 netdevice notifiers

Mainline DSA dropped the DSA notifier API that QSDK 14.x uses:

  src/init/ssdk_init.c:1714:14: error: implicit declaration of function
    'dsa_slave_dev_check'; did you mean 'dsa_user_dev_check'?
  src/init/ssdk_init.c:1719:73: error: 'struct dsa_port' has no member
    named 'master'
  src/init/ssdk_init.c:1760:22: error: 'DSA_NOTIFIER_PORT_LINK' undeclared
  src/init/ssdk_init.c:1763:59: error: invalid use of undefined type
    'struct dsa_notifier_link'
  src/init/ssdk_init.c:1862:17: error: implicit declaration of function
    'register_dsa_blocking_notifier'

Mappings:
 - dsa_slave_dev_check()  -> dsa_user_dev_check()   [rename]
 - dp->cpu_dp->master     -> dsa_port_to_conduit(dp) [rename; the
   dsa_port union now names the CPU-port netdev 'conduit']
 - DSA_NOTIFIER_PORT_LINK -> netdevice notifier NETDEV_CHANGE filtered
   with dsa_user_dev_check(), with netif_carrier_ok() replacing
   info->link.  Registration stays gated on the same legacy chip
   versions (MHT/AR8337/AR8327), so ipq95xx/APPE never runs it.

Classification: 6.12 移除的 API，主线已有替代（netdevice notifier）。

Also fix the missing-prototype warnings in this file: include fal_uk_if.h
for ssdk_cleanup(), keep qca_ar8327_phy_linkdown() external (ref_port_ctrl.c
calls it) with a local prototype, and give the remaining file-local
helpers internal linkage.

